  "title": "The White Peak Rover",
  "date": "2025-06-03",
  "excerpt": "Built on the Mercedes Sprinter 170 AWD chassis, the White Peak Rover blends serious off-road muscle with thoughtfully designed interior living. The foundation includes an Agile Off Road RIP kit with Fox shocks, all-terra",
  "body": [
    "Built on the Mercedes Sprinter 170 AWD chassis, the White Peak Rover blends serious off-road muscle with thoughtfully designed interior living. The foundation includes an Agile Off Road RIP kit with Fox shocks, all-terrain tires, and a matte black CA Tuned front bumper fitted with D-rings and a Warn 12S winch. Exterior lighting, a Lost Saguaro rear tire carrier, Tuff Skin spray liner, and a Starlink mobility kit ensure this van is ready for remote travel year-round.",
    "Inside, the van features 800Ah of lithium battery power, 400W of solar mounted to the SCA pop top, and a 3000W pure sine inverter. Paired with dual DC-DC chargers and shore power, the system is engineered to support off-grid living for extended periods. A full kitchen setup includes an induction cooktop, Isotherm fridge with freezer, undermount sink, butcher block counters, and a dedicated Zuvo water purification unit. The tiled indoor shower and rear outdoor rinse station add comfort and flexibility, supported by a 33-gallon fresh water tank and 4-gallon electric water heater.",
    "Comfort meets function with a queen memory foam bed, swivel driver and passenger seats, and an Alpine Van Works foldaway bench seat that converts into an additional bed. The pop top roof sleeps two more and features ambient LED lighting, a removable ladder, and full bug netting—ideal for high-altitude nights or warm summer trips. The ceiling is finished in natural-stained wood, matched with light-accented leather pulls and Pure Rubio Monocoat counters to bring a clean, alpine-inspired aesthetic to the build.",
    "From dual T-vent windows to blackout coverings, every detail in the White Peak Rover is tailored for extended, all-terrain travel. The van includes an onboard ARB air compressor, secure gear storage with a heavy-duty pullout tray, and a magnetic rear-door shower curtain system. Designed for high elevation and backcountry versatility, this build is ideal for travelers who need rugged performance without sacrificing comfort or design."
  ],
